<script>
/*
 * PackOptimizer.solve(rows, capacityKg, mix, options?)
 * rows: { id, quantity, stock, weight (kg, <=3 decimals), price (yuan/unit) }.
 * mix: 0 = proportional/average allocation, 1 = the optimized endpoint.
 * options.fillFirst defaults to true: maximize reachable weight <= capacity,
 * then maximize sales revenue at that same weight (also maximizing yuan/kg
 * at that weight). Set false for the legacy maximum-revenue-first objective.
 * This does not claim the maximum revenue/weight ratio across different loads.
 * Only supplied rows participate. Underweight plans only add; overweight
 * plans only remove. No mutation of the supplied rows.
 * Throws an Error with code INVALID_INPUT, STOCK_EXCEEDED, or RANGE_EXCEEDED.
 * quality describes only the selected, direction-constrained endpoint:
 * exact (bounded knapsack) or
 * approximate (resource-limited heuristic), never an unsupported optimality claim.
 * Integer apportionment at the average/intermediate positions is a heuristic.
